Now I have a clear picture. `FileExplorer` uses `basePath` computed from `this.$project.abs_project_path` and calls `this.$api.files.list(path)`. It doesn't accept a `root` prop — I need to add one so it can be overridden externally, then pass `workspace.folder_path` from `WorkspaceFileEditor`.

### Analysis & Pre-Thinking

- **Core Requirements**: Allow `FileExplorerPanel` (and by extension `FileExplorer`) to start navigation at `workspace.folder_path` instead of the project root.
- **Strategic Approach**:
  1. Add a `root` prop to `FileExplorer` — when provided, it overrides `basePath`.
  2. Add a `workspace` prop to `FileExplorerPanel` and pass `workspace.folder_path` down to `FileExplorer`.
  3. In `WorkspaceFileEditor`, replace the custom file-tree sidebar with `FileExplorerPanel`, passing the workspace.
- **Target Files**:
  - `src/components/filebrowser/FileExplorer.vue` — add `root` prop, override `basePath`
  - `src/components/filebrowser/FileExplorerPanel.vue` — add `workspace` prop, pass root to `FileExplorer`
  - `src/components/workspaces/WorkspaceFileEditor.vue` — use `FileExplorerPanel` instead of the custom tree

